## Lifecycle

This resource owns one explicit catalog binding. The delivery catalog must
already contain a compatible, authorized and enabled channel and target. Use
explicit channel and target UUIDs; name lookup and target discovery are not
supported. Unavailable bindings remain managed.

Changing the delivery channel or target replaces the binding because the API has
no on-call binding update operation. Create requires an active owner. Writes
have no revision precondition. Refresh and import use the exact scoped detail
read. Inactive owners do not hide retained bindings or prevent authorized
cleanup.

Destroy deletes only the binding; the delivery channel and target remain. A
schedule that references the binding can block deletion; remove that reference
explicitly. HTTP failures retain state. A confirmed `404 not_found` during
refresh removes the resource from state.

## Permissions

Requires `team_oncall_channel_catalogs.read`,
`team_oncall_channel_catalogs.create` and `team_oncall_channel_catalogs.delete`
in the owning team, plus access to the explicit delivery channel and target.
Service accounts require explicit native grants.
